01:02:10,909 --> 01:02:16,909
Bumblebee (stylized as BumbleBee and sometimes marketed as Transformers: Bumblebee) is a
2018 science fiction action film based on the Transformers toy line character.

13
01:07:21,818 --> 01:07:27,818
Directed by Travis Knight and written by Christina Hodson, it is the sixth
installment in the Transformers film series and a prequel to the 2007 film.

14
01:12:32,727 --> 01:12:38,727
It stars Hailee Steinfeld, John Cena, Jorge Lendeborg Jr.,
John Ortiz, Jason Drucker, and Pamela Adlon.

15
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
Set in 1987, the film follows Bumblebee being sent to Earth for
refuge and befriending a teenage girl named Charlie.

16
01:22:54,545 --> 01:23:00,545
The film premiered on December 3, 2018, at the Sony Center in Berlin, and was
released in the United States on December 21, by Paramount Pictures.

17
01:28:05,454 --> 01:28:11,454
It received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised its action sequences,
Steinfeld's performance, Knight's direction, visuals, and the 1980s setting.

18
01:33:16,363 --> 01:33:22,363
It was a box office success, grossing $468 million against a
production budget between $102–135 million.

19
01:38:27,272 --> 01:38:33,272
It was followed by Transformers: Rise of the Beasts in June 2023.

